theta_l-,theta_r+ = y- (x forces cancel)
theta_l+,theta_r- = y+ (x forces cancel)
theta_l-,theta_r- = x- (y forces cancel)
theta_l+,theta_r+ = x+ (y forces cancel)

x(theta_l,theta_r) = 0.5r_m(theta_l + theta_r)  (1mm of left displacement and 1mm of right displacement should be 1mm of nozzle displacement)
y(theta_l,theta_r) = 0.5r_m(theta_l - theta_r)

x'(theta_l,theta_r) = 0.5r_m(theta_l' + theta_r') 
y'(theta_l,theta_r) = 0.5r_m(theta_l' - theta_r')

We choose a state vector:
x_ = [theta_l', theta_r', theta_l, theta_r, i_ml, i_mr, x, y]^T
x_' = [theta_l'', theta_r'', theta_l', theta_r', i_ml', i_mr', x', y']^T

theta_l''(u_ml) = J_m tau_l
with tau_l = K_m i_ml
with i_ml' = (1/L_m)(u_ml-R_m i_ml), i_ml(0)=0

-> f(x_):
theta_l'' = J_m K_m i_ml
theta_r'' = J_m K_m i_mr
theta_l' = theta_l'
theta_r' = theta_r'
i_ml' = (1/L_m)(u_ml-R_m i_ml)
i_mr' = (1/L_m)(u_mr-R_m i_mr)
x' = x'
y' = y'

The input u is the motor voltages: u = [u_ml, u_mr]^T, B would be an 8x2 matrix (A 8x8)

So far we have not yet modeled the inertia of the toolhead, which has to be added to the model.














